[FEN "r2r2k1/p4ppp/1p1qpn2/2p5/2PP3Q/5N2/PP1R1PPP/R5K1 w - - 0 17"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r2r2k1/p4ppp/1p1qpn2/2p5/2PP3Q/5N2/PP1R1PPP/R5K1_w_-_-_0_17"]

{ He is doubling both rooks on the d column, aimed straight at your queen. Where does she want to go? }
17. Rad1 { Both his rooks now sit on the d column, staring at your queen. Find the move that tidies everything up. [%csl Rd6] } 17... Qc7 { Queen to c7: off the d column, and guarding both f7 and e5 at once. Nothing is hanging anywhere any more. [%csl Gc7][%cal Gc7f7][%tail] } (17... cxd4 { You open the position while you are still cramped, and that is exactly what his rooks were hoping for. } 18. Rxd4 Qc7 19. Ne5 { His pieces come pouring in. Worse for you. [%csl Rd4] }) (17... Rf8 { A rook move, and the queen is still sitting right on the column. } 18. Ne5 a6 19. Qf4 { Slightly worse for you: the queen never left the column, so the pressure never let up. }) (17... Qc6 { Off the column, but the f7 pawn is now loose. } 18. Ne5 Qc7 19. Qf4 { You end up going to c7 anyway. Equal. }) (17... Qb8 { Off the column, but far too far back to help. } 18. Ne5 Qc7 19. Qf4 { Back to c7 next move regardless. Equal. }) (17... Qe7 { Off the column, and f7 stays covered too. Also playable. } 18. Ne5 Qc7 { And you go to c7 anyway. }) (17... Ne4 { The knight jumps in, and the queen simply takes it. } 18. Qxe4 { A whole knight, gone. [%csl Re4] }) 18. h3 18... h6 19. Rd3 19... cxd4 20. Rxd4 20... Re8 { The other rook comes to e8. Both sides now have a rook on the open column, nothing hangs anywhere, and the position is dead level. [%csl Ge8] } 0-1
